{"title":"2024 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/4/a84addc076f56690a8812c52cfba1d89306b8557.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^n = 1000^{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"104\" height=\"17\" />, what is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/9/179676fa2ce50870d48d5a2bc0b7066f8404e255.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 1000 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 60 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 2000 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 300 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 102$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"488\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/2/7e21074365c6d164aca24ee1e8f11d442d494549.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^{3} = 1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"88\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/2/5824816b04404f3a9e921df5c7a6040cf36ac3b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a^{b})^{c} = a^{bc}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"85\" height=\"22\" />, so we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/5/e25a0eda5a65f0e9abb809a02be68ad47a60ee5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^{n} = 1000^{20} = (10^{3})^{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"182\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/d/64d9aa50a6a06a856c54a957720d0a1fe9fbbc4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^{n} = 10^{3 \\times 20} = 10^{60}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"159\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>The bases are equal to each other, meaning that the exponents must be equal to each other. This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63ce617815f2fea61da5c29b830a2d24badccf28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = \\boxed {\\textbf {(B) } 60}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"101\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Fermat\" title=\"2024 CEMC Fermat\">2024 CEMC Fermat</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Fermat_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 CEMC Fermat Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Fermat_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 CEMC Fermat Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2024 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" 